  "id": "just-noticeable-difference",
  "term": "just noticeable difference",
  "definition": "In this historical psychophysics context, a just noticeable difference is the smallest change in sensation that can still be detected, and it may be taken as a unit for measuring sensation. In the account linked to Fechner’s law, such detectable differences are treated as proportional to the size of the stimulus.",
